    "turn_text": "essentially yet while we we were for lowering the corporate tax rate just at twenty one percent right we thought that was excessive we're seeing all the share by backs the biggest windfall is to shareholders who stocks are going up and up and up yet they throw a few bonuses to people but what you can get back in the cut to Medicare and Social Security, because with PEGO, you have to cut once you have a deficit. So we could see cuts to major middle-class programs. We would roll that back, we'd restore the top rate on the top 1% of earners. So those of you who make over $450,000, yes, this would apply to you. But for the 99% of other Americans, you would be covered still and okay. And we would use that to come up with the $1 trillion infrastructure package that America was promised and I alluded to it a little bit but this This $1.5 trillion is going to require some cuts to Medicare and Social Security. Those are middle-class programs that people buy into. Right. But that's 70% of the budget between Medicare and Social Security and Medicaid. And under PEGO, if you have a deficit, you have to cut. They're automatic cuts. And one of the fancy, dancy tricks of this reform was to have it apply starting in 18 so that the cuts wouldn't have to come until 19 after the election. Right.",
